          "text": "[[EV_005]] [[EV_006]] [[EV_007]]"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "CLIENT",
          "text": "[[EV_008]]"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
          "text": "[[EV_009]] [[EV_010]]"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "CLIENT",
          "text": "[[EV_011]]"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
          "text": "Thank you, Elaine. Before we finish, you mentioned you'd be travelling soon. How would you prefer us to arrange future calls while you're away?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "CLIENT",
          "text": "I'm going to Japan with my family next month. We'll be moving between a few places, so please send me an appointment message first rather than calling unexpectedly."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
          "text": "Certainly. We can use the usual appointment channel. Would you prefer to leave the next appointment until you're back, rather than fitting a call around the trip?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "CLIENT",
          "text": "Yes, after I'm back is better. I don't want to be taking calls while we're on a train or trying to find the hotel. I'll message when I'm settled."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
          "text": "That's fine. For appointments back in Singapore, is the morning generally easier, or would an afternoon slot work better with your office schedule?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "CLIENT",
          "text": "Late morning usually works best. My staff handle the opening routine, and afternoons tend to fill up with supplier meetings. Just give me a bit of notice."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
          "text": "I'll note that preference for scheduling. Enjoy the family trip, Elaine, and thank you for making time today."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "CLIENT",
          "text": "Thanks, Marcus. Good to get the appointment done before the office gets busy. Have a good day. Bye."
